[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> /teach-code I know react, but I'd like to learn Flutter from this codebase.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 15.2s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Initial assessment requires understanding the codebase. Examining project files including docu...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ls -la)\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[12D\u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 4 files \u001b[37m(MISSION-FORMAT.md, README.md, GLOSSARY.md, +1)\u001b[m\n\u001b[64D\u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m \u001b[37m(find lib test -type f)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 10s\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  This repository is an \u001b[1mElectronics Parts Tracker\u001b[m (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk95f02d1a8c9d10c3;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_comprehension/pubspec.yaml\u0007pubspec.yaml\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkedae070749023f2a;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_comprehension/GLOSSARY."]
[0.000, "o", "md\u0007GLOSSARY.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007) built with \u001b[1mFlutter\u001b[m, \u001b[1mRiverpod\u001b[m\r\n  (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkdfd880c2ff438c3e;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_comprehension/lib/catalog/catalog_provider.dart\u0007catalog_provider.dart\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007), \u001b[1mFreezed\u001b[m (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk890951b12aeb2ff2;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_comprehension/lib/catalog/catalog_models.dart\u0007catalog_models.dart\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007), an \u001b[1mLCSC API client\u001b[m (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkca797864b003f3ba;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_comprehension/lib/lcsc/lcsc_client.dart\u0007lcsc_client.dart\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007), and \u001b[1mMaterial UI\u001b[m\r\n  (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkdda91a19ac30635b;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_comprehension/lib/ui/workbench_screen.dart\u0007workbench_screen.dart\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007)—all of which map cleanly onto React concepts you already know (components/hooks, immutable\r\n  state & reducers/Zustand/Redux, TypeScript interfaces, and Testing Library).\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  We'll "]
[0.000, "o", "set up the interactive course inside \u001b[94m./tutorial/\u001b[m so the root project stays untouched. Before I draft\r\n  \u001b[94mtutorial/MISSION.md\u001b[m and the first lesson, let's clarify your goal one step at a time:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[1mWhat does success look like for you at the end of this course?\u001b[m For example:\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mRebuild & master this app from the ground up\u001b[m — progressively reconstructing the Parts Tracker in \u001b[94m.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94m/tutorial/apps/\u001b[m (from Dart data models and Riverpod state up to the full workbench UI and widget tests) so you can\r\n  build new Flutter apps with the same stack.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mRead, modify, and extend this specific codebase\u001b[m — learning enough Flutter, Dart, and Riverpod through targeted\r\n  slices of this repo to confidently ship new features or changes to it.\u001b[K\r\n  3.\u001b[K\r\n⢿ \n\n\n\u001b[?2026l"]
